text:
Pasal 2
Penyelenggaraan pencegahan dan penanggulangan kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak, dilaksanakan berdasarkan asas :
a. penghormatan terhadap hak-hak perempuan dan anak;
b. keadilan dan kesetaraan gender;
c. non diskriminasi dalam pemberdayaan perempuan dan anak; d. kepentingan yang terbaik bagi perempuan dan anak; dan e. pemulihan hak sosial dan ekonomi bagi perempuan dan anak yang  mengalami tindak kekerasan atau penelantaran.

translated_text:
Article 2
The implementation of prevention and handling of violence against women and children is carried out based on the principles of:
a. respect for the rights of women and children;
b. gender justice and equality;
c. non-discrimination in the empowerment of women and children;
d. the best interests of women and children; and
e. restoration of social and economic rights for women and children who experience acts of violence or neglect.

text:
Pasal 4
Tujuan penyelenggaraan pencegahan dan penanggulangan kekerasan  terhadap perempuan dan anak, meliputi :
a. mencegah tindak kekerasan atau penelantaran terhadap perempuan dan  anak termasuk perdagangan orang;
b. menghapus segala bentuk kekerasan dan eksploitasi terhadap perempuan  dan anak;
c. melindungi dan memberikan rasa aman bagi perempuan dan anak; d. memberikan pelayanan kepada perempuan dan anak korban tindak  kekerasan, pelapor, dan saksi;
e. memfasilitasi dan melakukan mediasi terhadap sengketa rumah tangga  untuk mewujudkan keutuhan rumah tangga yang harmonis dan sejahtera;  dan
f. mengupayakan perolehan ganti rugi/kompensasi atas kerugian yang  diderita korban dari pelaku kekerasan.

translated_text:
Article 4
The objectives of organizing the prevention and handling of violence against women and children include:
a. preventing acts of violence or neglect against women and children, including trafficking in persons;
b. eliminating all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
c. protecting and providing a sense of security for women and children;
d. providing services to women and children who are victims of acts of violence, as well as to reporters and witnesses;
e. facilitating and conducting mediation of domestic disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household; and
f. seeking to obtain damages/compensation for losses suffered by victims from perpetrators of violence.

CHAPTER III
VIOLENCE
Article 5
(1) Forms of violence against women and children include:
a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. neglect;
e. exploitation; and/or
f. other violence.
(2) Physical violence as referred to in paragraph (1) letter a includes acts that result in pain, injury, wounds or disability to a person's body, miscarriage, unconsciousness and/or cause death.
(3) Psychological violence as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b includes acts that result in fear, loss of self-confidence, loss of ability to act, feelings of helplessness and/or severe psychological suffering to a person.
(4) Sexual violence as referred to in paragraph (1) letter c includes:
a. acts in the form of sexual harassment;
b. forced sexual intercourse;
c. forced sexual intercourse in an unnatural or unwanted manner; and/or
d. forced sexual intercourse with another person for commercial purposes and/or certain purposes.
(5) Neglect as referred to in paragraph (1) letter d includes:
a. acts that result in the failure to fulfill a child's needs properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after a child as appropriate, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts of neglecting a person within the household scope, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to an agreement or contract they are obligated to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to that person; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence by restricting and/or prohibiting decent work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.
(6) Exploitation as referred to in paragraph (1) letter e includes:
a. acts that exploit economically or sexually with the intention of benefiting oneself or others;
b. acts with or without the victim's consent which include but are not limited to prostitution, forced labor or services, slavery or similar practices, oppression, extortion, utilization of physical, sexual, reproductive organs, or unlawfully removing or transplanting organs and/or body tissues or exploiting the labor or abilities of a person by another party to obtain benefits both material and immaterial; and/or
c. any form of utilization of sexual organs or other body organs of the victim to obtain benefits, including but not limited to all activities of prostitution or indecency.
(7) Other violence as referred to in paragraph (1) letter f includes:
a. threats of violence include: any unlawful act in the form of speech, writing, images, symbols, or body movements, whether with or without using means that cause fear or restrict a person's fundamental freedom; and
b. coercion, includes: a situation where a person/victim is ordered to do something in such a way that the person does something contrary to their own will.

text:
BAB IV
HAK-HAK PEREMPUAN DAN ANAK KORBAN KEKERASAN
Pasal 6
(1) Setiap perempuan dan anak yang menjadi korban kekerasan fisik,  eksploitasi atau perdagangan orang berhak mendapatkan perlindungan  dan pelayanan.
(2) Perlindungan dan pelayanan pada korban sebagaimana dimaksud pada  ayat (1) meliputi :
a. pengaduan atau permohonan perlindungan dari yang bersangkutan; b. penanganan secara rahasia atau penempatan korban pada lokasi dan  rumah yang aman dan dirahasiakan keberadaannya untuk  menghindari intimidasi dan ancaman;
c. pelayanan medis/penanganan kesehatan berupa perawatan dan  pemulihan luka atau kondisi fisik korban oleh tenaga medis dan  paramedis;
d. pelayanan medikolegal untuk pembuktian dibidang hukum; e. perlindungan oleh aparat penegak hukum;
f. pemberian informasi seputar hak dan kewajiban hukum pada korban  atau wali korban serta identifikasi kejadian;
g. penanganan berkelanjutan sampai tahap rehabilitasi;
h. pendampingan secara psikologis untuk memulihkan kondisi traumatis  korban dan mengembalikan kepercayaan diri korban;
i. bantuan pendampingan untuk proses hukum dan perolehan hak  ganti rugi atau kompensasi;
j. jaminan atas hak-hak yang berkaitan dengan status sebagai anggota  keluarga maupun anggota masyarakat (reintegrasi sosial); dan k. pelayanan kemandirian ekonomi berupa pelatihan keterampilan dan  memberikan akses ekonomi agar korban dapat mandiri.
(3) Dalam hal korban adalah seorang anak, selain mendapatkan hak-hak  sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2), juga mendapatkan hak-hak khusus  meliputi:
a. hak atas penghormatan dan penggunaan sepenuhnya untuk  kelangsungan hidup, tumbuh dan berkembang;
b. hak pelayanan dasar;
c. hak perlindungan yang sama;
d. hak bebas dari berbagai stigma;
e. hak mendapatkan kebebasan; dan
f. hak mendapatkan ganti kerugian dari pelaku.

translated_text:
CHAPTER IV
RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE
Article 6
(1) Every woman and child who becomes a victim of physical violence, exploitation or human trafficking has the right to obtain protection and services.
(2) Protection and services for victims as referred to in paragraph (1) include:
a. complaints or requests for protection from the person concerned;
b. confidential handling or placement of victims in safe locations and houses whose whereabouts are kept confidential to avoid intimidation and threats;
c. medical services/health treatment in the form of care and recovery from injuries or physical conditions of victims by medical personnel and paramedics;
d. medicolegal services for evidence in the legal field;
e. protection by law enforcement officials;
f. provision of information regarding legal rights and obligations to victims or guardians of victims as well as identification of incidents;
g. continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage;
h. psychological assistance to restore the traumatic condition of victims and restore the self-confidence of victims;
i. assistance support for legal processes and obtaining the right to damages or compensation;
j. guarantee of rights related to status as family members and community members (social reintegration); and
k. economic independence services in the form of skills training and providing economic access so that victims can be independent.
(3) In the event the victim is a child, in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in paragraph (2), also obtains special rights including:
a. the right to respect and full enjoyment for survival, growth and development;
b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to equal protection;
d. the right to be free from various stigma;
e. the right to obtain freedom; and
f. the right to obtain compensation from the perpetrator.

text:
Pasal 8
(1) Kewajiban dan tanggung jawab Pemerintah Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud  dalam Pasal 7 huruf a, meliputi:
a. melaksanakan kewajiban perlindungan perempuan dan anak dari  tindak kekerasan yang ditetapkan oleh pemerintah;
b. menetapkan kebijakan, program dan kegiatan perlindungan  perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan;
c. melakukan kerjasama dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan  perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan;
d. memberikan dukungan sarana dan prasarana pelaksanaan  perlindungan perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan;
e. menyediakan rumah singgah untuk perempuan dan anak korban  kekerasan;
f. mengalokasikan anggaran penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan  dan anak dari tindak kekerasan sesuai kemampuan keuangan daerah;  dan
g. membina dan mengawasi penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan  dan anak dari tindak kekerasan.
(2) Pelaksanaan kewajiban dan tanggung jawab sebagaimana dimaksud pada  ayat (1), secara teknis dilaksanakan secara terpadu oleh SKPD terkait.

translated_text:
Article 8
(1) The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 7 letter a, include:
a. implementing the obligations for protection of women and children from acts of violence as stipulated by the government;
b. establishing policies, programs and activities for protection of women and children from acts of violence;
c. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. providing shelters for women and children victims of violence;
f. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with regional financial capacity; and
g. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(2) The implementation of obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be technically implemented in an integrated manner by related SKPD.

Article 9
(1) The obligations and responsibilities of the community as referred to in Article 7 letter b, shall be implemented in the form of community participation.
(2) The form of community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:
  a. establishing family partners at the kelurahan/village level by the community;
  b. establishing women and children protection units within community organizations;
  c. conducting socialization of women's and children's rights independently;
  d. providing first aid to victims; and
  e. reporting to the competent authority if violence against victims occurs in their environment.
(3) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by individuals, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, the private sector, and mass media.
(4) The form of community participation as referred to in paragraph (2), shall be implemented responsibly in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations.

Article 10
(1) The obligations and responsibilities of family and parents toward children as referred to in Article 7 letter c and letter d are in the form of:
   a. nurturing, caring for, educating and protecting children;
   b. preventing the occurrence of marriage at an early age;
   c. ensuring the continuity of children's education in accordance with the children's abilities, talents and interests; and
   d. in the event that parents do not exist or their whereabouts are unknown or due to a certain reason, cannot carry out their obligations and responsibilities, then the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1) may be transferred to the family as the child's guardian, which shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of the applicable laws and regulations.

